[32m+[m[32m# CASEOPS timeline workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep timeline CSVs in the ignored `caseops-local/` directory or outside the checkout.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe timeline tool uses Python's standard library, works offline, and never opens[m
[32m+[m[32msource URLs. No dependency installation is needed for this command.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mmkdir -p caseops-local[m
[32m+[m[32m# Copy your timeline CSV into caseops-local using your file manager.[m
[32m+[m[32mpython scripts/caseops_timeline.py caseops-local/timeline.csv --check[m
[32m+[m[32mpython scripts/caseops_timeline.py caseops-local/timeline.csv[m
[32m+[m[32mpython scripts/caseops_timeline.py caseops-local/timeline.csv --scope civil[m
[32m+[m[32mpython scripts/caseops_timeline.py caseops-local/timeline.csv --scope criminal[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe exact CSV header is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```csv[m
[32m+[m[32mdate,docket_scope,event,source_status,source_url[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDates use `YYYY-MM-DD`; scopes are `civil`, `criminal`, or `system`.[m
[32m+[m[32mAll five fields are required. Source URLs must use HTTPS without embedded[m
[32m+[m[32mcredentials. Quote fields containing commas, quotes, or newlines using normal CSV[m
[32m+[m[32mquoting. Events are displayed chronologically; the source file is never rewritten.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStatuses are preserved verbatim. A scheduled appearance does not establish its[m
[32m+[m[32moutcome, and receipt of an order does not establish the attachment's contents.[m
[32m+[m[32mCivil and criminal entries retain their separate scopes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSource links are omitted from display unless you pass `--include-links`. Event[m
[32m+[m[32mdescriptions and statuses can still contain private information: the default[m
[32m+[m[32mreport is for local review and is not an automatically sanitized publication.[m
[32m+[m[32m`--check` prints only the event count and input-file SHA-256.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe digest identifies the CSV's exact bytes, including line endings and ordering.[m
[32m+[m[32mIt does not authenticate source communications or establish the truth of an event.[m
[32m+[m[32mChanging bytes changes the digest. A GitHub commit containing a digest is a[m
[32m+[m[32mreference point; checking it requires the corresponding original file.[m
[32m+[m
